cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below."
title: "EIGER: label-free discovery of regionally coordinated DNA methylation"
abstract: >-
  EIGER identifies differentially methylated regions without requiring
  predefined sample groups, by segmenting the genome into blocks in which
  neighbouring CpGs co-vary across samples. Version 2 adds pairwise-complete
  estimation, a scale-free discovery statistic, a locality-breaking null and a
  region-level empirical false discovery rate. The originally published caller
  is retained and runnable via --legacy. Version 2.0.1 corrects the direction
  and tied-cutoff handling of the region-level false discovery rate estimator
  and adds finite-null uncertainty quantification via simultaneous Garwood
  Monte Carlo bounds on each region's q-value.
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Milne-Clark
    given-names: Toby
version: "2.0.1"
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/tobymilnec/EIGER"
keywords:
  - DNA methylation
  - differentially methylated regions
  - whole-genome bisulfite sequencing
  - false discovery rate
  - unsupervised
